WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.940
<b>I want to be connected
A</b>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.180
Toi!

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.610
What is this?

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:36.760
This is you guys a moment ago.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.020
Look how desperate they are, 
after they betrayed you.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.270
The outside of the circle of this 
world is deep down below here.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.150
The place where there's no beginning, 
no ending and no connecting.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.530
You're giving up your connections 
before you go there.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.350
Giving up my connections?

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.390
It's easy.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.030
Just use that gun...

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.300
to shoot your past self.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.730
What is this?

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.930
This is bad.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:34.990
Toi is heading outside the circle, 
erasing his past self as he goes, kero.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:39.490
If he does, everything will be erased...

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.850
Both your connection with him 
and his entire existence.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.240
We have to stop him.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:02.140
That's it. Throw it all away.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:06.140
You'll never have been hurt if 
it never happened to begin with.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.390
He's gone here, too.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.830
How far back has he gone?

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.300
Four years ago.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:23.300
If he's really intent on cutting 
his connection with us,

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.910
he must be going to the day 
he gave me this miçanga.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.540
Kazuki...

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.860
You remembered.

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:31.420
Yeah.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:37.420
The three of us connected that day, 
thanks to this miçanga he gave us.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.930
We still have time as long 
as the miçanga is still here, kero.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.680
Otter...

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.930
Begone, you poison-spewing pests.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.290
Shit!

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.340
Keppi.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.340
Leave this to me.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.950
You two go on ahead, kero.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.980
Otter...

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.490
I let two rats get away.

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.710
You're an especially crazy kappa.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.210
We're going to end this today, kero.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.150
I'm not letting you have 
your way any longer, kero!

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.750
Otter?

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.170
The fact that you would tell me what
to think after you'd become so hopeless

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:30.230
that you cut away your despair is laughable.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.450
Otter...

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:37.650
Now it's time for you to become 
completely engulfed by otter despair!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:46.550
This is our beginning.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.500
That's right.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.770
Shoot your younger self,
 and the connection is gone.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.630
After that, you're outside the circle.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.630
<b>Azumabashi</b>

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.070
I wanted to become a soccer player.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.140
<b>Sobakyu</b>

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.140
Dad, Mom, and my brother were there.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:15.150
I had no doubts about the future.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:21.650
But Dad and Mom died, and you shot a man.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:32.040
But just one person, 
my brother, held my hand.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.100
You're still talking about that?

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.170
I only used you.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.420
I was fine with that.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:49.430
Giving things up, doing bad things...
It all had to be done.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.430
What's the matter?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.690
Are you clinging to your connections now,
 after you've come so far?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.190
This is a connection that I chose for myself.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.210
So I'm giving it up with my own hands.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.580
The bad ones are the ones 
who survive in this world.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.850
Which are you?

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.100
Otter...

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:22.090
Goodbye, Nii-san.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:27.340
Now I can end it all.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.190
Kazuki!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.370
Why are you here?

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.980
To take you back.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.240
I'm tired of you two.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:55.570
The miçanga!

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.330
Dadadadadadadadadadada...

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.250
Darkness.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.050
Dark Keppi.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.750
You were an imposter!

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.760
I...

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.690
I won't let go of our connection.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:18.390
Even if you cut me off, 
I'll keep reconnecting.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:26.020
Dadadadadadadadadadada...

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.700
Darkness.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.700
